    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jonathan Aranda** stands out as our premier start with a score of 70.47. His matchup against Bieber is highly favorable; the combination of a weak 5.10 xERA starter and an advantageous #2 spot in the order elevates his production ceiling significantly. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a high-floor play at 65.73, and while his matchup against Bradley is slightly tougher, his elite capacity for stolen bases against a pitcher with a slow delivery provides an essential boost in our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Gleyber Torres** and **Geraldo Perdomo** provide solid mid-tier production near the 60-point threshold; both are hitting in favorable lineup spots, though **Gleyber Torres** faces a slight penalty due to platoon dynamics despite the soft opposing starter.\n\nOur benching process prioritized efficiency over raw output, with **Gavin Sheets** being the most notable exclusion. His 35.12 score fell well below our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold, largely due to a difficult matchup against Sale. While **Gavin Sheets** typically provides power, the 19% reduction in expected performance based on Sale\u2019s elite skill set made him an easy sit to preserve our limited game caps. We are also managing the absences of **Cal Raleigh**, **Bryce Harper**, and **Will Smith**\u2014the latter currently sidelined on the IL\u2014which further condensed our available options for the day.\n\nAs we monitor the remainder of the roster, including **Masyn Winn** and **Ryan Waldschmidt**, we remain cautious about the overall team context. **Masyn Winn** offers subtle value through his speed, which remains vital for LawDog's 5x5 objectives, yet his 53.61 score reflects a more neutral matchup against Pfaadt. No weather-related risks have been flagged, but as we continue to track the status of depth pieces like **Lawrence Butler**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Taylor Ward**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Z